So, we will work on Majority element now. Majority element is that element in an array that
appears more than n/2 times. For example, a given array is [1,2,2,1,1,1]. Here, n=6, so n/2=3
So, the element '1' appears more than 3 times in the array. So, 1 is the majority element 
here. There are three ways to find out the majority element inside an array. The three ways are:
i) Brute-force way
ii) Efficient way
iii)Moores-voting algorithm


iii)Moores-votinng algorithm:
Moores voting algoritm says that, if we consider a 'frequency' to determine the number
of times an element repeats inside an array, then, the frequency of the majority element
will be the maximum. According to this algorithm, we will set everytime the value of
frequency to 0, if there is a new element in the array. If the element is same as the
previous one, we will do freq++ and if its different, we will do freq--. 

